Z||000000||JoeFiero||04-20-2001||04:08 PM||||I've got an '87 coupe with the L4 that runs good but not great. It runs best when cold, but when warm it seems to hesitate or miss and feels like its towing a boat when you accelerate...  I've replaced the plugs and wires but not the coils.  I'm also pretty sure I need to replace the throttle position sensor, cause it will idle fast and slowly drop down.<P>Any thoughts on general tuning??||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||04-20-2001||04:25 PM||||My brother car acted the same way always sputtering and skipping at idle until he got a major tuneup. He replaced all the filters, plugs, GM wires and now it runs great. Don't buy any other ignition wire other than GM.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Posthumane||04-21-2001||03:59 PM||||Joe, my 84 2m4 has the EXACT same problem. i replaced the plugs, fuel filter, checked timing, etc. Gonna check the wires and coil next... let me know if you find a fix.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-21-2001||08:22 PM||||read the stuff in my cave before you mess around at random. <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Ogre's Fiero Cave</A><P>those probems are unlikely to be the ignition. (beyond wires or plugs.)<P>More likely to be:<P>MAP<P>MAT<P>TPS<P>Vac Leak.<P>Fuel Vapor can. (Could be hooked up wrong or bad.)||||reg||1
